# Container-build context exclusions. Keeps the layer-1 COPY from
# pulling local build artefacts and committed-but-irrelevant
# tooling into the image, both of which would invalidate the
# `go mod download` cache layer on every code change.

bin/
dist/
testdata/

# Dev-time scratch directories that shouldn't ship in any image.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.local.yaml

# Service install artefacts from a host-side `bridge init`. These
# would never be useful inside a container and could leak host
# paths into a multi-stage build context if accidentally COPY'd.
*.plist
*.service

# Operator-side state from a host-side `bridge init` / `bridge serve`.
# `data/` carries the SQLite manifest + paired-device token hashes;
# `tls/` carries the self-signed cert and its private key; `bridge.yaml`
# is the operator's config with API tokens. None should ever land in
# a container build context — the builder stage's `COPY . .` would
# otherwise pull them in, slowing cache invalidation AND making a
# future careless multi-stage COPY a credentials-leak risk.
data/
tls/
bridge.yaml
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Source-control + CI metadata. `.git/` invalidates the cache layer
# on every commit; `.github/` references repository secrets that are
# never needed inside an image.
.git/
.github/

# Misc.
coverage.out
*.test
